A||||14||fiero56||Need opinions on my '86SE||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||12-14-2000||01:02 AM||||I have an '86SE right now and am deciding what I want to do with it. I really like the silver paint it currently has, but am thinking of reversing the color scheme and painting it like a black '85GT. Black body, silver ground effects.<BR>Another thing is, I have always wanted to own an '84 Indy, but with so few ever produced, and the few that are left go for a high premium. I am thinking about painting my '86SE to match an '84 Indy on the exterior. I really like the Fiero body style in white, and the Indy just looks that much better. Paint the wheels, do the pin-striping, the fender badges and door decals, etc. This does present a problem though. I have always been strongly against making something it isn't(basically turn my SE into an Indy, which it isn't). I have several terms that come to mind, but won't post them. The interior would not be stock anyway, so I wouldn't care that it wouldn't match. I wouldn't want people to think it was an original Indy anyway.<P>Any thoughts?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TOF00021#2.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||12-14-2000||01:53 AM||||If you paint it simular to an Indy that would be fine but once you put on the decals or Indy logo's then you'd be "making it something it was not". I always thought about using the SD4 paint scheme. White on top and dark metallic blue/grey on bottom. The blue/grey starts about 1" above the front scoop (on an SE/GT) and continues around the car at the same height. These are seperated by a thin red pinstripe. It looks good but my car is presently black and I like that too. The next one I get I'll paint like noted above but I want an 84 coupe and the blue/grey will start at the molding and go down. The molding will be painted red.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-14-2000||07:03 AM||||I like it the way it is. <P>I was thinking along the same lines as you about doing the Indy wannabe thing to my 85GT.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-14-2000||10:06 AM||||orange would be nice..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||12-14-2000||11:05 AM||||I vote for monochromatic silver, but retain the black mirror and rub strip.  Get the 88 GT color scheme on an aero notchback...(drool)||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||12-14-2000||11:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>I have always been strongly against making something it isn't (basically turn my SE into an Indy, which it isn't). I have several terms that come to mind, but won't post them. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmm ... me thinks this was directed at my yellow fender decal!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>RATS!  In my attempt to be funny, I forgot to post my suggestion.<P>I like Chad's idea.  Do the monochromatic scheme - including painting the moldings and mirrors (but leave the heat exhaust vents and the air intake black).  I think Torch Red from the C5 would look awesome - especially with the "hi-tech" 14" rims painted black like mine!  Paint the brake calipers red as well and finish it all off with <B>lightly</B>-tinted windows and tail lights.<P>Man, I'm drooling!!!!!  All I can say is ....... <B>SWEET!!!!!!!!!!!!!</B><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
