Z||000007||fiero56||12-14-2000||12:06 PM||||Thought of this idea this morning. What if I painted the car like a black '85GT(black body, silver ground effects), and put on white Indy door decals. It would never be confused with a real Indy by Fiero enthusiasts, and would be different than the norm. Just another thought.<P>I need to see what the mono-chromatic scheme looks like on aero-notchback, haven't seen many like that. Red isn't a bad idea, but I am thinking of going with a darker color. But everytime I see WTIII's red '85GT, I always change my mind and decide red would be nice.<P>So, I need a few (smallish for loading speeds) pictures of, black '85GT, and mono aero notchback paint scheme, any colors.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87ECO5||12-14-2000||12:37 PM||||If you had your 2001 calendar, you'd find a PERFECT example on the month of September.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Here it is:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Unknown1.jpg">   <P>If I remember correctly, someone said this was an '84.  So, if that's true, and factoring in the aero-notchback styling, does that mean this was a Pace car?  Ironic, isn't it!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Notice the black roof - a la Stealth, Eclipse, etc.<P>Mmmmm ....... sorry, more drool!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||2M4 Dale||12-14-2000||01:20 PM||||56 I think that I like your SE like it is...Even though I have an effinity for Black cars !!!<P>I really like that red car with the black top Scott !!! TOO COOL Looks like an idea for my sons 86 SE. I'll have to show him the pic.<P>Scott, I like your "Ferarri like" badges. (Ferrari wannabe).....lol||||reg||6
Z||000010||87ECO5||12-14-2000||02:16 PM||||Hell, if you think about it, my car is the epitome of "being something it's not!"  It's a Ferrari wannabe with the fender logo and engine detailing.  It's a Formula wannabe with the combination body style and black wheels.<P>And, it's soon to be a Corvette wannabe!<P>How do they say it?  Imitation is the sincerest form of flattery!<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||fiero56||12-14-2000||03:10 PM||||You're car is still a Fiero Scott. It may have similarities to others, is not a a wannabe' as far as I am concerned. If you had done the black wheel thing, put "Formula" stickers on the doors, done the dual exhaust, put the v'6 guages in, etc, then it would be. The "Ferrari"(sp???) sticker is really cool, thats one of my favorite things on your coupe. The engine is nice too, Fiero red. <BR>I'm curious about the 'Vette thing though.<P>Nobody has any ideas about my black Indy Fiero? I think that would be cool, might do it that way. I like that pic Scott, but my 14" tech wheels wouldn't cut it with a paint job that bright.<BR>Need more pictures.||||reg||1
